            "review_text": "Stevefamlux\nDudelange, Luxembourg73 contributions\n0\nA good taste of Korea\nAug 2014 • Couples\nRecently opened, this restaurant, located on Le Van Sy street in district 3, belongs to Gogi house who have 2 more restaurants in Ho Chi Minh City and another 3 in Hanoi.\nMy Vietnamese wife and I, decided to give it a try, as it is located near my family's home. We both love Korean food and were not to be disappointed. \nArriving without a reservation, the place was well visited, but the waitress managed to get us a table by the window. Service was very swift and friendly. I cannot say too much about the staff's knowledge of English as I let my wife place the order in Vietnamese. My Vietnamese is such that I never go hungry or thirsty when in Vietnam, however I have a tendancy to get lazy in speaking when my dear wife is around .\nThe menu card has a very good variety of dishes as well as drinks. Cool Sapporo draught beer (without ice) is served in pitchers up to 1.3 liters.\nWe settled for a squid salad as a starter and chose the beef barbecue with Kimchi salad and rice as a main course, on first hand because it looked so good on the table next to us, on second hand it happened to be on promotion.\nThe portions served were big and the meat was very tender and tasty. The Kimchi salad was so delicious that I actually ordered a second plate. The grill was at all times surveyed by our charming waitress, who would care that no slice stayed on too long and when the temperature cooled down a bit, a busy young man exchanged the charcoal immediately. A good exhaust system over the actual grill prevents the cooking fumes from getting into your clothing.\nAll in all we had a great dinner. but even the best of meals come to an end, and they are usually followed by a bill. Dining for around 800.000 VND, including drinks and taxes, is good value for money.\nWe will surely visit this restaurant again.\n\nI would like to point out that the retaurant is non-smoking. Transportation should not be a problem, as Gogi house is located on a main street.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 5, 2014\nGolden Gate Restaurant Group\nThank you for taking the time to review our restaurant. It is a pleasure to hear that Gogi House met your expectations. We hope to see you again, and wish you all the best !!!\nRead more\nWritten July 10, 2015\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
